  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> of a liquid of specific heat capacity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c\"></span> flows every second through a heater of power <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>. What is the difference in temperature between the liquid entering and leaving the heater?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mc}{P}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"273+\\frac{mc}{P}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{P}{mc}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"273+\\frac{P}{mc}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
